{"id":"000W2R","title":"City Lights","author":"Jorava","solvedCount":16,"difficulty":2,"rating":"75 %","firstSeen":"2026-11-17T22:57:06+00:00","posted":"Heute, 18:26 Uhr","rules":"Dynamic fog (with street lamps), white kropki, XV, skyscraper.\n\nMade for the CTC discord November Monthly Prompt \"Illuminations\".\n\nAlso an homage to one of my favorite films.\n\nSolve in Sudokupad\n\n-----\n\nRules:\n\nNormal sudoku rules apply. Place the digits 1-9 in every row, column, and 3x3 box.\n\nKropki:\nDigits paired by a white dot are consecutive. In lower class sections of the city (rows 7, 8, and 9), there is a negative constraint: Consecutive digits may not be together without a white dot chaperoning them. This applies up to the border between middle class and lower class (rows 6 and 7).\n\nXV:\nDigits paired by X sum to 10. Digits paired by V sum to 5.\n\nSkyscrapers:\nNumber outside the grid tells you how many digits it sees in its row or column, where higher digits block the view to smaller digits behind them (e.g. if 6 is closer to the Skyscraper clue than 5, the clue can't see the 5, but if 7 is behind the 6, the clue can see the 7).\n\nCity Lights:\nMost of the city is hidden under darkness. Placing a correct digit in a cell reveals darkness from that cell. If you place a correct digit in a street lamp, it shines light along the roads in all 4 directions, dispelling the darkness. Even digits are houses, and block the light from entering or passing through their cells.","solutionCode":"Column 5","tags":["Sudoku","Kropki","XV (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/axe5mtdi8m","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/axe5mtdi8m","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-17T22:57:06+00:00"}